{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":85815,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"f3b1f7c3-5879-46f2-855c-5b6f53757d21","total_cost_usd":0.8337415,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":63101,"cache_read_input_tokens":20101,"output_tokens":5835,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":63101,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5835,"cache_read_input_tokens":20101,"cache_creation_input_tokens":63101,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":63101},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":46686,"outputTokens":22,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.046796,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":5835,"cacheReadInputTokens":20101,"cacheCreationInputTokens":63101,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7869455000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"agent\":\"playtester\",\"verdict\":\"targets_missed\",\"summary\":\"The crew's own config never leaves the pad in simulation and its central ablation claim inverts under measurement — every band and load lands cheapest on a single committed entry, with skimming a pure surcharge, and the exploration grid says a genuine multi-pass optimum is not reachable anywhere in the design's world space.\",\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"ascent_fails_all_bands\",\"gdd_ref\":\"2.3.6\",\"claim\":\"game_params asserts base dv = 2391*ln(1520/900) = 1254 m/s against a ~950 m/s suborbital ascent, and fuel_tank t1 opening the low band at 1548 m/s.\",\"measured\":\"All three ascents in the verification sweep report reached=false, why='crashed on ascent', fuel_remaining_kg=0, fuel_margin_pct=0 — suborbital, low and high alike. The descent half of the sweep still flew, so the flight model is live; it is the powered ascent that does not close. The exploration grid satisfies bands_reachable in 60.5% of 2916 configurations, so an ascent that works exists in the space — the crew's own point is not one of them.\",\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"kind\":\"tuning\"},{\"id\":\"ablation_optimum_is_one_pass_everywhere\",\"gdd_ref\":\"2.3.1\",\"claim\":\"ablation.optimal_skims claims 1/1/2 skims for suborbital/low/high, and the params' cost_curve puts the low-band minimum at index 1 (29.88%) and the high-band minimum at index 2 (42.82%), i.e. a 2-4 committed-pass descent is the cheap path.\",\"measured\":\"cheapest_pass_count = 1 in all nine band x load descents. Ablation rises monotonically with pass count in every one: suborbital full hold 13.5 -> 15.5 -> 16.3 -> 17.0%, low full hold 11.8 -> 15.7 -> 16.9 -> 17.5%, high full hold 11.7 -> 17.6 -> 18.9 -> 19.9%. The high band's second pass costs +5.9 points where the params predicted a saving of 5.6. Measured plate cost also falls with altitude (13.5% suborbital vs 11.7% high at the optimum) — the inverse of the 20/30/43 the params assert.\",\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"kind\":\"design\"},{\"id\":\"skim_benefit_saturates_but_never_pays\",\"gdd_ref\":\"2.3.1\",\"claim\":\"§4.5 risk 1 predicts the U-shaped ablation curve may not tune to a 2-4 pass optimum; params assert skim_heat_multiplier [1, 0.93, 0.89, 0.88].\",\"measured\":\"The grid settles it: skim_benefit_saturates is satisfied by 89.5% of configurations while skimming_cools_the_entry holds in only 45.1%, and no configuration in the top-scoring set shows a per-skim gain that keeps improving — the measured multipliers are step functions ([1, 0.44, 0.44, 0.44] at radius 60000) or near-flat decays ([1, 0.962, 0.924, 0.888]). At the crew's own point the measured arrays are [1, 0.951, 0.897, 0.684] suborbital, [1, 0.977, 0.955, 0.934] low, [1, 0.984, 0.968, 0.954] high — a third skim buys 1.6-4.6% off peak heat at a cost of 1-3 extra hours of simulated flight (high band: 1.22h direct vs 4.15h at 3 skims). The saving is real and too small to pay the fatigue toll. This is the design problem §4.5 named, not a mistuned constant.\",\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"kind\":\"design\"},{\"id\":\"committed_entry_depth_dominates_skim_count\",\"gdd_ref\":\"2.3.1\",\"claim\":\"The design frames pass count as the player's primary heat lever.\",\"measured\":\"Entry depth moves peak heat far harder than skim count. High band, 0 skims: entry_peak_heat 163.1 at entry_depth 0, 139.1 at 18000, 93.8 at 36000 — a 1.74x span from depth alone. Three skims at fixed depth move it only 163.1 -> 155.7 (1.05x). Low band shows the same shape: 131.5 / 114.0 / 82.0 across depth versus 131.5 -> 123.0 across skims. The interesting decision the design wants from pass count already lives in how deep the committed entry is flown.\",\"severity\":\"significant\",\"kind\":\"design\"},{\"id\":\"cargo_mass_barely_moves_the_flight\",\"gdd_ref\":\"2.3.5\",\"claim\":\"§2.3.5: 'a full hold roughly doubles the rocket's mass at starting storage size', and mass is the lever that makes greed cost something.\",\"measured\":\"Measured full_hold_mass_ratio = 1.11 (kg_per_slot 16.23, full_hold_kg 97.4 against 900 kg dry). Consequences at the optimum: touchdown 3.39 m/s empty vs 3.57 m/s full (+5.3%), peak heat 65 vs 69 suborbital, ablation 11.9% vs 13.5%. The params' own balance_notes concede this ('1.16x, not 2x') and file it under catalog_concerns. The grid says greed_costs_something is satisfiable in 46.9% of configurations, so this is reachable — it needs mass, and the params cannot reach it because dry mass is floored by the ballistic-coefficient note while slot count is fixed at 6.\",\"severity\":\"significant\",\"kind\":\"tuning\"},{\"id\":\"unstaged_pass_is_the_scarce_target\",\"gdd_ref\":\"2.3.1\",\"claim\":\"Shallow unstaged braking passes before staging are the technique the whole descent is built on; unstaged_heat_multiplier 3.0 is set specifically to preserve it.\",\"measured\":\"The crew's config satisfies it — unstaged shallow-pass peak heat 62 suborbital and 71 low, both under the 100 cargo-damage threshold. But it is the rarest target in the grid at 15.4% satisfaction, and every one of the six top-scoring 60000 m worlds fails it with unstaged_peak_heat 478-502. This is the one thing the current world gets right that the highest-scoring alternatives do not, and it is the reason not to chase the 60 km/9.81 configurations despite their score of 7.\",\"severity\":\"significant\",\"kind\":\"design\"},{\"id\":\"touchdown_speed_undershoots_its_own_claim\",\"gdd_ref\":\"2.3.2\",\"claim\":\"landing.descent_speed_full_hold_ms = 4.8, sitting deliberately just under the 5 m/s soft-landing line so a greedy hold is near the edge.\",\"measured\":\"Measured full-hold touchdown is 3.57 m/s at every band; empty is 3.39. That is 26% under the claimed figure and 29% of margin below the hard-landing line, so no reachable load in the shipping slice can produce a hard landing. soft_landing = true in all nine descents. The sweep flags that parachute area is not a parameter at all and had to be inferred (6.0 m2 from the 4.8 m/s claim), which is itself the defect — the claim and the model are anchored to each other rather than measured.\",\"severity\":\"significant\",\"kind\":\"tuning\"},{\"id\":\"difficulty_falls_with_altitude\",\"gdd_ref\":\"2.3.7\",\"claim\":\"§2.3.7: reentry speed and heat scale with the altitude returned from, so value and risk rise together; heat_index 83/100/119 by band.\",\"measured\":\"At each band's cheapest descent the high band is the *coolest* return: peak heat 65 (high, full hold) vs 65 (low) vs 69 (suborbital), and ablation 11.7% (high) vs 11.8% (low) vs 13.5% (suborbital). The ordering only reverses at deep committed entries (163.1 high vs 131.5 low vs 100 suborbital at entry_depth 0), so the risk curve exists but the optimal-play curve inverts it. The grid satisfies difficulty_rises_with_band in 32.1% of configurations — uncommon but far from impossible, so this is reachable by tuning.\",\"severity\":\"significant\",\"kind\":\"tuning\"},{\"id\":\"ballistic_coefficient_is_the_binding_quantity\",\"gdd_ref\":\"4.5\",\"claim\":\"The Researcher quotes 171 kg/m2 staged empty and 305 kg/m2 staged full, inside the real capsule range.\",\"measured\":\"The sweep measures staged beta 171.4 and unstaged 734.7 — the staged figure matches, the unstaged is 734.7 against the Researcher's asserted 1959, so the pre-stage hull is 2.7x less slippery than the baseline derivation claims and shallow unstaged passes brake harder than designed. Across the grid, the top configurations that satisfy skimming cluster at low beta (11.1 to 44.4 kg/m2) and all fail unstaged survivability, while every config that survives unstaged sits at beta 133-1333 and fails skimming. The two targets are opposite ends of one quantity; no world in the grid satisfies both.\",\"severity\":\"significant\",\"kind\":\"design\"},{\"id\":\"fuel_margin_is_the_rarest_tuning_target\",\"gdd_ref\":\"2.3.6\",\"claim\":\"The band gate is that tank and thruster upgrades buy altitude with a sane reserve at each tier.\",\"measured\":\"fuel_margin_sane is satisfied in 19.5% of the 2916-config grid — the second-rarest target after unstaged survivability, and rarer than bands_reachable (60.5%). Reaching a band and reaching it with a usable reserve are separately hard, and best_score across the entire grid is 7 of 8 with no configuration scoring 8. There is no world in this space where every design target holds at once.\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"kind\":\"design\"}],\"proposed_changes\":[{\"path\":\"flight.thrust_n\",\"current\":11000,\"proposed\":16000,\"reason\":\"Every band crashes on ascent at 11000 N; raising liftoff TWR from 1.81 to 2.63 puts it in the band the grid's top configurations occupy (2.6) and buys back gravity losses, at the cost of a steeper gravity turn the human will have to fly.\"},{\"path\":\"flight.fuel_burn_kgs\",\"current\":4.6,\"proposed\":5.4,\"reason\":\"Holds exhaust velocity near 2960 m/s at the raised thrust so the Isp stays honest for a scrapyard engine rather than inflating dv for free; it shortens burn time and tightens the reserve.\"},{\"path\":\"flight.fuel_capacity_kg\",\"current\":620,\"proposed\":780,\"reason\":\"Restores the dv lost to the higher burn rate and gives the suborbital ascent a measurable margin instead of 0%; it raises liftoff mass and lowers TWR slightly, and pushes the tank t1/t2 upgrade values up with it.\"},{\"path\":\"ablation.cycle_toll_base_pct\",\"current\":0.53,\"proposed\":0.15,\"reason\":\"The measured skim saving is 1.6-4.6% of peak heat while the current toll charges 0.53% growing at 1.5x per cycle, which is why measured ablation rises monotonically with pass count; cutting the toll is the smallest move that lets a second pass ever pay, and it weakens the anti-feathering guard that the toll exists to provide.\"},{\"path\":\"ablation.cycle_toll_growth\",\"current\":1.5,\"proposed\":2.2,\"reason\":\"With a lower base toll, a steeper growth rate keeps feathering uneconomic past four cycles — this is the pair that has to move together, and it makes the penalty for over-skimming arrive abruptly rather than gradually.\"},{\"path\":\"ablation.optimal_skims\",\"current\":{\"suborbital\":1,\"low\":1,\"high\":2},\"proposed\":{\"suborbital\":0,\"low\":0,\"high\":0},\"reason\":\"Corrects the params to what the simulator measured — cheapest_pass_count is 1 in all nine descents — so the Auditor is checking against a true claim; it concedes that the 2-4 pass optimum is not currently realised.\"},{\"path\":\"landing.descent_speed_full_hold_ms\",\"current\":4.8,\"proposed\":3.57,\"reason\":\"The claimed 4.8 is not measured anywhere; the sweep flies 3.57 m/s at full hold in every band, and stating the measured value removes the circular inference the sweep had to make about parachute area.\"},{\"path\":\"landing.parachute_area_m2\",\"current\":null,\"proposed\":6,\"reason\":\"The sweep had to infer canopy area from the descent-speed claim because no such field exists; publishing it breaks the circularity so descent speed becomes a measurement rather than an assumption.\"},{\"path\":\"landing.parachute_drag_coefficient\",\"current\":172.6,\"proposed\":96,\"reason\":\"Cuts descent speed margin so the full base hold lands near 4.8 m/s as designed and a greedy hold can actually cross the 5 m/s line; it makes the Parachute upgrade load-bearing and makes early hard landings possible, which is the intent of 2.3.2.\"},{\"path\":\"baseline.reentry.drag_coefficient_hull\",\"current\":0.35,\"proposed\":0.22,\"reason\":\"Measured unstaged beta is 734.7 against the baseline's asserted 1959, so the pre-stage hull brakes harder than the derivation claims; lowering hull Cd restores the slipperiness that makes pre-stage shallow passes a distinct technique, at the cost of a longer powered descent if a player brakes propulsively.\"},{\"path\":\"baseline.planet.sea_level_density_kgm3\",\"current\":0.6,\"proposed\":0.35,\"reason\":\"Thins the air so the committed entry is less dominant relative to skims and unstaged passes stay survivable — the grid's unstaged_pass_survivable target (15.4% satisfaction) clusters at low density; it raises terminal velocity and forces the parachute change above.\"}],\"confidence_notes\":[\"The ascent failures are the load-bearing uncertainty in this report. All three bands report the identical signature — reached=false, fuel_remaining_kg=0, fuel_margin_pct=0 — while the params' own hand-computed dv (1254 m/s against a ~950 m/s suborbital ascent) says the suborbital band should close with reserve. Either the simulator's ascent guidance is a naive vertical climb with no gravity turn, or the thrust genuinely does not close. I have proposed thrust and tank changes on the assumption the number is real, but the human should confirm the ascent profile before flying them; if the guidance is the defect, my first three proposals are unnecessary and the config's flight section is already sound.\",\"The simulator is a point mass with a perfect pilot. It has no attitude error, so off_retrograde_penalty is never exercised and the cosine heat rule in 2.3.1 is untested by anything here. It has no debris collisions, no tether physics and no EVA model, so every claim in the params about shear, latch jerk and towing (the whole 2.3.4 block) is unmeasured by this sweep and I have made no finding about it either way.\",\"The ablation finding is measured but its interpretation depends on a model choice I cannot see: the sweep's ablation figures rise monotonically with pass count, which means its per-pass toll is charged before any skim benefit is credited. That is consistent with the params' own formula, so I read the contradiction as real rather than an artefact — but if the simulator applies skim cooling only to the committed entry and not to total integrated heat, it will systematically undervalue skimming. Worth one look at the ablation accumulator before acting on cycle_toll_base_pct.\",\"The exploration grid scores worlds, not the crew's world. Its 15.4% unstaged-survivability rate and 19.5% fuel-margin rate are statements about the sampled space (4 radii x 3 gravities x 3 densities x 3 areas x 3 masses x 3 fuel fractions x 3 TWRs), and that grid does not contain the crew's actual point — radius 200000 and gravity 4.0 are both outside the sampled values. The satisfaction rates are therefore good evidence about which targets are structurally hard and poor evidence about how close the current config sits to each.\",\"My density and hull-Cd proposals move the baseline rather than game_params, which is a larger blast radius than a tuning nudge: every derived figure in the Researcher's document — the dv-per-pass table, the terminal-velocity arithmetic, the atmosphere top — is computed from rho0 and would need recomputing. I propose them because the grid says the skimming/unstaged pair is controlled by ballistic coefficient and air density and cannot be fixed inside game_params, but they are the changes most deserving of a human's veto.\",\"No configuration in 2916 scored 8 of 8. The design's targets are not simultaneously satisfiable in the sampled space, and the two that conflict most directly — skimming cooling the entry and an unstaged pass being survivable — sit at opposite ends of ballistic coefficient. If that holds under a finer grid, §4.5's named fallback (flat per-pass ablation cost with a hard cap on passes) is the honest resolution, and it costs the U-curve rather than a pillar.\"]}","ttft_ms":83787,"ttft_stream_ms":1740,"time_to_request_ms":211,"type":"result","duration_ms":83806,"uuid":"f6411262-d74b-4c37-be72-4f246aa20299"}
